# PostgreSQL column alignment

Edit column order in `src/packages/database/src/schema/` only. Migrations are generated from schema — do not hand-edit SQL for alignment.

Read `src/packages/database/src/schema/README.md` before adding or reordering columns.

## Order within each `pgTable`

1. **8-byte** — `timestamp`, `bigint`, `doublePrecision`, …
2. **4-byte** — `integer`, `real`, `date`, `pgEnum`, …
3. **16-byte** — `uuid`
4. **1-byte** — `boolean`
5. **Variable-length last** — `text`, `varchar`, `bytea`, `json`, `jsonb`, …

When changing columns, re-sort the **whole** list — do not append if it breaks alignment.

## Why

PostgreSQL pads fixed-width types to alignment boundaries. Mixed column widths waste space in every row.

See [docs/DEV.md](../../docs/DEV.md) for migration workflow.
